# WhatsApp-Style Frontend — PRD & Requirements

## Purpose
Create only the frontend UI for a WhatsApp-inspired chat web application. The provided WhatsApp screenshot is the visual reference.

## 1. Project Scope
Build a polished, responsive frontend only. Use mock/static data and frontend state. No backend, database, API, authentication, Supabase, or Render.

## 2. Core Frontend Features
- **Chats**: Chat list, live search, individual chat screen, message bubbles (incoming/outgoing), message input, emoji picker, attachments menu, reactions, audio message player, send-message interaction with realistic automated mock reply.
- **Groups**: Create group UI, group chat, add users, remove users, change group admin, admin permissions and role badges.
- **Channels**: Channel list, channel view, verified badges, follow/unfollow toggle, mock channel posts with view counts and reactions.
- **Status**: Status list (My status + recent updates), full-featured status viewing UI with animated progress bars, captions, and reply bar.
- **Calls**: Calls list with call history (incoming, outgoing, missed), and interactive incoming/outgoing calling overlay UI with call timer, mute, camera, and end call actions.
- **User Profile**: Profile information, profile-picture placeholder, edit-profile UI (name, about, status, avatar), and light/dark theme toggle.

## 3. Design Requirements
- Use the supplied screenshot (`Reference/Wattsapp screenshot 1.png`) as the main visual reference.
- Recreate its overall layout, structure, spacing, typography, colors, navigation rail, chat list, icons, and visual style.
- Use Lato as the main font (load from local `Lato/` directory and Google Fonts fallback).
- Responsive on desktop, tablet, and mobile (collapsible sidebars and drawers).
- Use reusable, component-based frontend code.
- Use realistic mock names, messages, groups, and channels.
- Do not copy or expose real personal information from the screenshot.

## 4. Technical Requirements
- Frontend only.
- No backend.
- No database.
- No Supabase.
- No Render.
- No APIs.
- No authentication.
- Zero build tools required; works cleanly in any modern web browser.
